OL,3,GNEWSAGreens deputy leader sorry over
OL,4,Alack of bin strike knowledge
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe deputy leader of the Green Party
OL,7,Fhas apologised to the residents of
OL,8,FBirmingham after admitting she did not
OL,9,Fknow enough about the city's near
OL,10,Ftwo-year bin strike to comment on why
OL,11,Fit was yet to be resolved.
OL,13,FRachel Millward said she had not been
OL,14,Fup to date with the dispute when
OL,15,Fquestioned about it during an interview
OL,16,Fwith BBC Radio WM - part of a series of
OL,17,F12 consecutive interviews with regional
OL,18,FTV and radio stations across England.
OL,23,APub: 02-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,352,350,200,160,0,100
